<title>GERMANY: German April 1997 metals output detailed.</title>
<headline>German April 1997 metals output detailed.</headline>
<dateline>ESCHBORN, Germany 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German copper and lead output rose in Jan/April 1997 while zinc and aluminium output was lower than in the same 1996 period, official figures showed on Friday.</p>
<p>Base metals data from the state statistics office Bundesamt fuer Wirtschaft (BAW) showed output of semi-finished non-ferrous metals products in the four months was higher than a year earlier.</p>
<p>The rate of increase over the same 1996 period in Jan/April had increased in all semis over Jan/March.</p>
<p>Castings figures were also mostly higher, with the exception of lead.</p>
<p>The report gave the following details, in tonnes --</p>
<p>METALS OUTPUT	April 97 Jan/April 97  Cumulative pct change</p>
<p>							    over Jan/April 96</p>
<p>primary aluminium	46,349  186,947		  -  2.8</p>
<p>electrolytic copper    48,827  197,215		  +  1.6</p>
<p>zinc			 26,605  104,035		  -  4.2</p>
<p>refined lead	     22,465   76,418		  + 23.4</p>
<p>SEMI-FINISHED MTLS April 97 Jan/April 97  Pct change over 1996</p>
<p>aluminium		 163,376  578,487		  + 17.9</p>
<p>copper		    152,518  537,053		  + 11.1</p>
<p>zinc			 16,901   57,359		  +  8.8</p>
<p>lead			  4,986   16,342		  + 16.3</p>
<p>nickel			2,083    7,026		  + 15.4</p>
<p>METALS CASTINGS    April 97  Jan/April 97 Pct change over 1996</p>
<p>aluminium		  49,092  180,390		  +  6.7</p>
<p>copper			7,256   26,702		  +  3.4</p>
<p>zinc			  5,813   21,879		  +  0.3</p>
<p>lead			    511    1,954		  - 14.7</p>
<p>Semis and castings figures included alloys. Nickel and tin castings data were not given.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
